    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters August 1st with a lineup headlined by **Mickey Moniak**, whose elite 75.75 efficiency score makes him our premier play. Facing Luinder Avila, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to park factors and a favorable platoon matchup, coupled with a prime #2 lineup spot. **James Wood** follows closely with a 69.82 score; despite a 37% rain risk, his elite .424 xwOBA against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez creates significant offensive upside. Meanwhile, **Austin Riley** (67.16) remains a strong play against Miles Mikolas, as his score is bolstered by the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an enticing environment for our stolen base-focused strategy, provided he avoids a mid-game rainout.\n\nOur bench logic was most severely tested by **Isaac Paredes**, who logged a 48.51 score but was ultimately squeezed out by our depth at corner infield and utility spots. While **Isaac Paredes** projected well against Jacob deGrom due to platoon advantages, the combination of deGrom\u2019s elite skill and the optimizer\u2019s preference for the high-ceiling platoon advantages of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Henry Bolte** against Framber Valdez kept him sidelined. We remain cautious of the volatility inherent in today's pending lineups, particularly for **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero**; while **Jose Caballero** benefits from a high platoon edge against David Peterson, his 9-hole projection and negative wind impact keep him firmly in the \"marginal\" start category. We are prioritizing players like **Corbin Carroll** and **Seiya Suzuki** despite their tougher matchups, as maintaining game caps remains a structural priority for the stretch run.",
